This software (the Highwatch Travel API, its command-line tool and their
documentation) is published in source form so that server owners can run it
themselves and read what runs on their servers. It is not open source.

You may:
1. Run this software yourself, on machines you own or rent, as the Travel API
   for a network of DayZ servers that you own or operate, with the Highwatch
   Travel mod.
2. Read and modify it for that use.
3. Keep private copies and backups, and fork it on GitHub as GitHub's terms of
   service allow, to keep your changes for your own network.

You may not:
1. Redistribute this software or any part of it, modified or not, in source
   or packed form (including as an archive, an installer or a container
   image), except a fork on GitHub as allowed above, or as Highwatch itself
   distributes it.
2. Offer it, or a service built on it, to other server owners: no hosting it
   for networks you do not own or operate, no reselling access to it.
3. Use it, or any part of it, with a mod other than Highwatch Travel, or to
   build a competing product or service.
4. Remove or alter this notice or the headers that refer to it.
5. Sell, sublicense, or lease it.

